###  https://purl.archive.org/nudging#basic_monocentric_city_model
<https://purl.archive.org/nudging#basic_monocentric_city_model> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                         <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Theory> ;
                                                                rdfs:comment "Basic monocentric city model assumes that all employment is located at the central point (central business district, or CBD) and all households have one worker. Household equilibrium in the model includes the condition that the marginal cost and marginal benefit of commuting distance are equal; the cost of one more mile of commuting equals the saving on housing expenses."@en ;
                                                                rdfs:label "basic monocentric city model" .


